  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, adapted from the Aura3D humanoid recipe. It typechecks, but I couldn't run `vite build` or view the scene, so the look and framing are untested. The robot is built from primitives with nested joint groups: hips, chest, head, both shoulders and elbows, both hips and both knees. That is 11 joints. An idle animation driven from `onFrame` moves the hips, chest and head, both arms and both legs with sine waves, so the pose changes over time. Lighting is a warm key light with shadows, a blue rim light and a magenta rim light, all on a dark background with a floor to catch shadows. A fixed perspective camera frames the whole robot, centred. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame callback and again after `app.ready()`.",
